  faqs={[
    { q: 'When should I start studying for board exams?', a: 'Ideally from the start of the school year, with steady weekly revision. If you are starting a structured plan now, 4 months before the first paper gives enough time for one learning pass, two revision rounds and plenty of sample papers.' },
    { q: 'How many hours should a Class 10 student study for boards?', a: 'Around 2.5–3 focused hours on school days and 5–6 hours on holidays in the final two months. Consistency matters more than marathon days. See <a href="/guides/how-many-hours-to-study-a-day/">how many hours to study a day</a>.' },
    { q: 'How many hours should a Class 12 student study for boards?', a: 'Around 3–4 focused hours on school days and 6–7 on holidays and study leave. If you are also preparing for an entrance exam, merge the two plans so common topics are studied once.' },
